# Build output and Gradle's own state. Copying either in would ship one
# machine's absolute paths and daemon registry into the image, and the build
# inside the container would then disagree with itself about where things are.
#
# THE PATTERNS ARE RECURSIVE ON PURPOSE. .dockerignore matches from the context
# root, so a bare `build` excludes ./build and nothing else -- it does not
# match app/build or core/build. With core/ added as a second build, the
# non-recursive form silently started copying 2.8MB of host output back in.
**/build
**/.gradle
**/.idea
**/*.iml
**/local.properties

# The APKs this image exists to produce.
artifacts
**/*.apk

.git
